 "page": [
  {
   "kind": "town",
   "label": "town",
   "section": "header",
   "text": "Warmholz · hamlet · germanic · threat frontier · route road · terrain river · seed sim-hamlet"
  },
  {
   "kind": "machine",
   "label": "historicalCharacter",
   "section": "identity",
   "text": "A settlement whose great advantage is that nothing has ever forced it to become anything in particular. It has kept its options, its neighbours, and its temper, and it regards all three as achievements, correctly, though few visitors see why"
  },
  {
   "block": "DS-GEN-13",
   "face": 0,
   "kind": "composed",
   "mount": "overview.market",
   "pool": "NO-MARKET",
   "section": "site",
   "text": "Nothing in Warmholz is arranged for buying and selling in quantity, which tells a stranger the essential thing about the place.",
   "vid": 1
  },
  {
   "block": "DS-GEN-17",
   "face": 0,
   "kind": "composed",
   "mount": "overview.institutions",
   "pool": "BARE",
   "section": "site",
   "text": "Nothing in Warmholz is official that could instead be somebody's job on the side.",
   "vid": 1
  },
  {
   "kind": "badge",
   "label": "crisis.label",
   "section": "crisis",
   "text": "Beast & Raider Threat"
  },
  {
   "kind": "machine",
   "label": "crisis.summary",
   "section": "crisis",
   "text": "Something in the surrounding region has grown bolder. Caravans are disappearing. A farmstead burned last week. Whether wolves, raiders, or worse. The settlement's defences are adequate for normal times, but these are not normal times."
  },
  {
   "kind": "machine",
   "label": "crisis.hook",
   "section": "crisis",
   "text": "The attacks are following a pattern that suggests coordination, not desperation. Someone is directing this (whether a rival lord, a beast of unusual cunning, or something stranger). The evidence is there for anyone who looks carefully."
  },
  {
   "block": "DS-STR-1",
   "face": 0,
   "kind": "composed",
   "mount": "overview.crisisBanners",
   "pool": "BEAST & RAIDER THREAT",
   "section": "crisis",
   "text": "Warmholz has pulled its stock and its people inward, and the ground it has given up is on the rolls as abandoned.",
   "vid": 4
  },
  {
   "block": "DS-STR-1",
   "face": 0,
   "kind": "composed",
   "mount": "overview.crisisBanners",
   "pool": "Overview's own section framing",
   "section": "crisis",
   "text": "Nothing here is urgent. The town's difficulties are chronic rather than acute, and it has the room to work on them.",
   "vid": 1
  },
  {
   "block": "DS-CND-1",
   "face": 0,
   "kind": "composed",
   "mount": "overview.activeConditions",
   "pool": "SEVERITY: critical",
   "section": "conditions",
   "text": "This is as far as Warmholz bends. Past this it is not the same settlement, and it is very near past this.",
   "vid": 1
  },
  {
   "block": "DS-CND-1",
   "face": 0,
   "kind": "composed",
   "mount": "overview.activeConditions",
   "pool": "DIRECTION: worsening",
   "section": "conditions",
   "text": "It is getting worse, steadily rather than suddenly; each season costs a little more than the one before.",
   "vid": 0
  },
  {
   "kind": "badge",
   "label": "prosperity",
   "section": "health",
   "text": "Poor"
  },
  {
   "kind": "badge",
   "label": "safetyLabel",
   "section": "health",
   "text": "Dangerous — Monster Threat"
  },
  {
   "kind": "badge",
   "label": "readiness",
   "section": "health",
   "text": "Vulnerable"
  },
  {
   "kind": "badge",
   "label": "foodSecurity",
   "section": "health",
   "text": "Secure"
  },
  {
   "block": "DS-GEN-3",
   "face": 0,
   "kind": "composed",
   "mount": "overview.systemsHealth",
   "pool": "prosperity: Struggling / Poor",
   "section": "health",
   "text": "Warmholz's year closes near enough to level that the closing is watched.",
   "vid": 1
  },
  {
   "block": "DS-GEN-3",
   "face": 0,
   "kind": "composed",
   "mount": "overview.systemsHealth",
   "pool": "safetyProfile.safetyLabel: head word in {Dangerous, Desperate}",
   "section": "health",
   "text": "What the watch at Warmholz records is a fraction of what happens, and the fraction is not chosen by the watch.",
   "vid": 2
  },
  {
   "block": "DS-GEN-3",
   "face": 0,
   "kind": "composed",
   "mount": "overview.systemsHealth",
   "pool": "economicViability.viable: true",
   "section": "health",
   "text": "Warmholz works on the terms it currently has, and the judgment is about those terms rather than about the town.",
   "vid": 3
  },
  {
   "block": "DS-GEN-3",
   "face": 0,
   "kind": "composed",
   "mount": "overview.systemsHealth",
   "pool": "defenseProfile.readiness.label: Vulnerable",
   "section": "health",
   "text": "Warmholz has less between itself and trouble than a town this size ought to.",
   "vid": 1
  },
  {
   "block": "DS-GEN-3",
   "face": 0,
   "kind": "composed",
   "mount": "overview.systemsHealth",
   "pool": "scores.military: CRITICAL",
   "section": "health",
   "text": "What protects Warmholz is that nobody has wanted it, and everyone here understands the arrangement.",
   "vid": 2
  },
  {
   "block": "DS-GEN-3",
   "face": 0,
   "kind": "composed",
   "mount": "overview.systemsHealth",
   "pool": "scores.monster: CRITICAL",
   "section": "health",
   "text": "Warmholz has no answer to what lives beyond its fields and nobody whose work it would be.",
   "vid": 1
  },
  {
   "block": "DS-GEN-3",
   "face": 0,
   "kind": "composed",
   "mount": "overview.systemsHealth",
   "pool": "scores.internal: WEAK",
   "section": "health",
   "text": "There is more going on in Warmholz than the watch troubles itself with, and it is not hidden particularly well.",
   "vid": 0
  },
  {
   "block": "DS-GEN-3",
   "face": 0,
   "kind": "composed",
   "mount": "overview.systemsHealth",
   "pool": "scores.economic: WEAK",
   "section": "health",
   "text": "There is nothing spare in Warmholz, and the absence of spare is what a careful eye notices first.",
   "vid": 1
  },
  {
   "block": "DS-GEN-3",
   "face": 0,
   "kind": "composed",
   "mount": "overview.systemsHealth",
   "pool": "scores.magical: CRITICAL",
   "section": "health",
   "text": "Warmholz keeps no practitioner, no arrangement, and no expectation of either.",
   "vid": 1
  },
  {
   "block": "DS-GEN-3",
   "face": 0,
   "kind": "composed",
   "mount": "overview.systemsHealth",
   "pool": "foodSecurity.label: Secure",
   "section": "health",
   "text": "Nobody in Warmholz thinks about food, which is the most that can be said for a town's food.",
   "vid": 1
  },
  {
   "kind": "machine",
   "label": "arrivalScene",
   "section": "situation",
   "text": "Warmholz buys arrows. The fletcher's is the busiest shop in the settlement, and the militia board outside the gate lists a standing bounty in terms that carefully avoid naming what it is for. A dozen buildings around a central green, most of them old. Half-timbered upper floors project above the busier lanes. A magelight lamp post marks the main gate. A mile marker, then a second, then the outlying farms of Warmholz begin. The settlement proper is still a quarter hour ahead."
  },
  {
   "kind": "machine",
   "label": "pressureSentence",
   "section": "situation",
   "text": "Warmholz has drawn its edges inward (fields left unworked, a mill standing idle) trading the charcoal it needs for a perimeter the able-bodied can actually hold."
  },
  {
   "block": "DS-GEN-6",
   "face": 0,
   "kind": "composed",
   "mount": "overview.origin",
   "pool": "road",
   "section": "origin",
   "text": "Warmholz is here because somebody, once, found this a reasonable distance from the last place.",
   "vid": 1
  },
  {
   "block": "DS-GEN-6",
   "face": 0,
   "kind": "composed",
   "mount": "overview.origin",
   "pool": "tier overlay: thorp / hamlet",
   "section": "origin",
   "text": "Warmholz is a handful of roofs with a reason, and the reason is usually the ground.",
   "vid": 1
  },
  {
   "block": "DS-REL-2",
   "face": 0,
   "kind": "composed",
   "mount": "overview.notableConnection",
   "pool": "flagDriven count zero",
   "section": "connection",
   "text": "The people of Warmholz are connected the way the people of any settled place are connected, and there is no more to say about it than that.",
   "vid": 2
  },
  {
   "block": "DS-GEN-7",
   "face": 0,
   "kind": "composed",
   "mount": "overview.warnings",
   "pool": "structuralSuggestions[]",
   "section": "warnings",
   "text": "A careful reader of Warmholz finds one loose end, and it is the kind that a single institution would tie off.",
   "vid": 2
  },
  {
   "kind": "roster",
   "label": "institutions",
   "section": "institutions",
   "text": "institutions: Resident smith (part-time), Carpenter (part-time), Hunter's lodge, Charcoal burner, Informal elder consensus, Access to parish church, Burial ground, Dwellings (17-80), Water source, Access to external mill, Subsistence farming, Common grazing land, Mine (open cast), Dairy farmer"
  }
 ],
